---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
import { LINKS, BOOK } from '../site.config';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Akshata Sawant: Lead Developer Advocate at Salesforce in London, co-author, speaker and MuleSoft community leader.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <Image src={headshot} alt="Portrait of Akshata Sawant" width={160} height={160} widths={[160, 320]} sizes="160px" class="photo" />
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I'm Akshata Sawant, a Lead Developer Advocate at Salesforce, based in London. I help developers and architects build secure, AI-ready integrations and agents, through writing, speaking and open-source examples.</p>
    <p>I have about nine years of experience in software, four of them at Salesforce. My work covers Agentforce, MCP, the Headless Experience Layer, Data Cloud Document AI and MuleSoft, and I build demos for keynotes at Dreamforce and TDX.</p>
    <p>Before Salesforce I was a Senior Software Engineer at EPAM Systems in London, and worked on integration and API projects at Apisero and Capgemini in India.</p>
    <p>I co-authored <a href="/book/"><em>{BOOK.title}</em></a>, now in its second edition. I've led MuleSoft meetups in Mumbai and London for more than seven years, and was a MuleSoft Ambassador from 2020 to 2022.</p>
    <p>Right now I'm building <a href="https://github.com/akshatasawant9699/sf-ops-agent">sf-ops-agent</a> in public: an eval-tested Salesforce ops agent.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Certifications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Salesforce Certified AI Associate</li>
    <li>MuleSoft Certified Integration Architect</li>
    <li>MuleSoft Certified Developer, Level 1</li>
    <li>Pragmatic Institute PMC Level I</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timeline</h2>
  <Timeline />

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>The best way to reach me is a message on <a href={LINKS.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
</Base>
<style>.photo { width: 160px; height: 160px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; margin: .5rem 0 1.25rem; }</style>
